WireGuard outbound: dial through the tunnel taken under the lock, and survive Close

FORK DEVIATION: a minimal fix, not upstream code. Upstream removed this race with the refactor
8626311 (#6287), which does not apply to the pin. processWireGuard returns the tunnel it read
under wgLock and Process dials through that value; a closed handler refuses new work; and
netBind.Close tolerates a second close.

